This repository is public so that the work in it can be READ. It is not open
source, and nothing in it is offered for reuse.

Read this before assuming anything: the absence of a familiar licence name is
deliberate. This is not MIT, not GPL, not Creative Commons. If you were looking
for permission to use something here, the answer is no by default and yes only
in writing.


1. WHAT YOU MAY DO

   a. View, read and study any part of this repository.
   b. Clone or fork it for the sole purpose of reading it, evaluating it, or
      preparing a contribution back to this project.
   c. Build and run the game locally, unmodified, to evaluate it.
   d. Quote short excerpts for commentary, review, teaching or criticism, with
      attribution — the kind of thing fair dealing and fair use already allow.


2. WHAT YOU MAY NOT DO

   Without prior written permission from the copyright holder, you may not:

   a. Copy, publish, redistribute, sublicense, sell or otherwise make available
      any part of this repository, in original or modified form.
   b. Use any part of it in another project, product or service, whether or not
      that project is commercial, free, or open source.
   c. Use any ART, SOUND, MUSIC or other creative asset from this repository for
      anything at all, in any medium, including as reference, as a base to trace
      or modify, or as part of a collection or asset pack.
   d. Run the generators in tools/ to produce art or audio for use outside this
      project. The generators and their output are one thing; a permission that
      covered the generator but not the sprite would be no permission at all.
   e. Use any part of this repository as training data for a machine-learning
      model, or to create a derived dataset, index or embedding intended for that
      purpose.

   This applies to every part equally — the C# in scripts/, the scenes, the
   generators in tools/, the design documents in .ai/, and above all the contents
   of assets/.


